# Ansible Vault Password File
#
# IMPORTANT: This is a template file. To use it:
# 1. Copy this file to .vault_pass in the same directory
# 2. Replace the placeholder text with your actual Ansible Vault password
# 3. Set proper file permissions: chmod 600 .vault_pass
#
# Purpose:
# This file contains the password used by Ansible Vault to encrypt and decrypt
# sensitive data in your Ansible playbooks and roles. It is used during deployment
# to both staging and production environments.
#
# Security Considerations:
# - NEVER commit the actual .vault_pass file to version control
# - Keep this password secure and limit access to authorized personnel only
# - Consider using different vault passwords for staging and production if needed
# - For production environments, consider using a more secure method like a key management service
#
# Usage:
# The .vault_pass file is referenced in ansible.cfg or via the --vault-password-file
# flag when running Ansible commands:
#
# Example:
#   ansible-playbook deploy.yml --vault-password-file=config/.vault_pass
#
# For more information on Ansible Vault, see:
# https://docs.ansible.com/ansible/latest/user_guide/vault.html

# Replace this line with your actual vault password
YOUR_ANSIBLE_VAULT_PASSWORD_HERE
